hadiths[648]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7163","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I do not eat while reclining."
"7164","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no reward for the one who does not intend it for reward."
"7165","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is none more jealous (ghayur) than Allah, and that is why He has forbidden indecencies, whether open or hidden; there is none to whom praise is more beloved than Allah, and that is why He praised Himself; and there is none to whom offering excuse is more beloved than Allah, and for that reason He sent down the Book and sent the Messengers."
"7166","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Castration is not permissible in Islam."
"7167","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I do not ride on purple, nor do I wear safflower-dyed clothing, nor do I wear a shirt hemmed with silk. Behold! The perfume of men is that which has fragrance but no colour, and the perfume of women is that which has colour but no fragrance."
"7168","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In Islam there is no helping one another in wailing (for the dead), nor slaughtering animals at the grave, nor is there shighar in Islam, nor is there jalab in Islam, nor janab; and whoever plunders is not one of us."
"7169","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is to be no secret taking of the spoils of war and no betrayal of trust."
"7170","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I do not count him a liar: the man who makes peace between people and says something by which he intends nothing but reconciliation, the man who speaks in war, the man who speaks to his wife, and the woman who speaks to her husband."
"7171","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware! As long as I am among you, let no one of you die without your informing me of it, for my prayer over him is a mercy for him."
"7172","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let me not find any of you reclining on his couch, when a command of mine reaches him, something I have commanded or forbidden, and he says: I do not know; we will only follow what we find in the Book of Allah."
"7173","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let me not find any of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a camel on his neck, grunting, saying: O Messenger of Allah, help me! And I will say: I have no power to do anything for you; I conveyed (the message) to you. Let me not find any of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a horse on his neck, neighing, saying: O Messenger of Allah, help me! And I will say: I have no power to do anything for you; I conveyed (the message) to you. Let me not find any of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a sheep on his neck, bleating, saying: O Messenger of Allah, help me! And I will say: I have no power to do anything for you; I conveyed (the message) to you. Let me not find any of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with a person on his neck, screaming, saying: O Messenger of Allah, help me! And I will say: I have no power to do anything for you; I conveyed (the message) to you. Let me not find any of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with pieces of cloth fluttering on his neck, saying: O Messenger of Allah, help me! And I will say: I have no power to do anything for you; I conveyed (the message) to you. Let me not find any of you coming on the Day of Resurrection with gold and silver on his neck, saying: O Messenger of Allah, help me! And I will say: I have no power to do anything for you; I conveyed (the message) to you."
"7174","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let me not find people from my Ummah coming on the Day of Resurrection with good deeds like the white mountains of Tihamah, and then Allah turns them into scattered dust. Behold! They are your brothers and of your own kind; they rise at night for worship just as you rise, but they are people who, when alone with what Allah has made sacred, violate it."
"7175","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""La ilaha illallah (there is no true god except Allah); indeed, death has its agonies."
"7176","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""La ilaha illallah (there is no true god except Allah)! Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near. Today an opening like this has been made in the barrier of Ya'juj"" - and he (peace and blessings be upon him) made a circle with his thumb and the finger next to it. It was said: ""Will we be destroyed while there are righteous people among us?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Yes, when filth becomes widespread."
"7177","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I do not touch the hands of women."
"7178","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No, by Allah! A mount upon which a curse has been laid shall not accompany us."
"7179","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no faith for the one who has no trustworthiness, and there is no religion for the one who does not keep his covenant."
"7180","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not go to soothsayers."
"7181","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no harm in exchanging one animal for two, hand to hand."
"7182","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no harm in wealth for the one who is God-fearing; health for the one who is God-fearing is better than wealth; and contentment of heart is among the blessings."
"7183","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no harm in exchanging wheat for barley, two for one, hand to hand."
"7184","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no harm; let a man help his brother, whether he is an oppressor or oppressed. If he is an oppressor, let him restrain him from oppression, for that is helping him; and if he is oppressed, let him help him."
"7185","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""An arif (tribal overseer) is necessary, but the arif is in the Fire."
"7186","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting while travelling is not righteousness."
"7187","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A hundred years will not pass while any living soul that is on the earth today remains."
"7188","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No woman should give anyone permission (to enter) in her husband's house without his permission."
"7189","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not call the adhan until the dawn becomes clear to you like this."
"7190","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not give permission to the one who does not begin with the greeting of salam."
"7191","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not hurt a Muslim by cursing a disbeliever."
"7192","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever a woman hurts her husband in this world, his (Paradise) wife from among the wide-eyed houris says: 'Do not hurt him, may Allah destroy you! He is only a guest with you; soon he will leave you and come to us.'"
"7193","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not eat onions."
"7194","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not eat with the left hand, for Satan eats with the left hand."
"7195","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not race ahead of the imam. When he says the takbir, say the takbir; when he says 'Wa la d-dallin', say 'Amin'; when he bows, bow; when he says 'Sami'a Allahu liman hamidah (Allah hears the one who praises Him)', say 'Allahumma Rabbana wa laka l-hamd (O Allah, our Lord, and to You be all praise)'; and do not raise (your heads) before him."
"7196","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not go ahead of me in bowing or in prostration, for however far ahead of you I get when I bow, you catch up with me when I rise; and however far ahead of you I get when I prostrate, you catch up with me when I rise. Indeed, I have grown old (and heavy)."
"7197","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman should not come close to another woman (and look at her beauty in such a way) that she then describes her to her husband as though he were looking at her himself."
"7198","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A heap of grain should not be sold for (another) heap of grain, nor should a heap of grain be sold for a specified measure of grain."
"7199","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not hate one another, do not turn your backs on one another, do not envy (and compete with) one another, and, O servants of Allah, be brothers to one another."
"7200","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not hate one another, do not sever ties with one another, do not turn your backs on one another, do not envy one another, and, O servants of Allah, be brothers to one another as Allah has commanded you. It is not lawful for a Muslim to shun his brother for more than three days."
"7201","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not buy dates until their ripeness becomes evident, and do not buy dates in exchange for dates."
"7202","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not buy fruit until its ripeness becomes evident and the blight (disease) has passed from it."
"7203","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Buy gold for gold only like for like, with no increase between them and no deferment."
"7204","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not be the first to greet the Jews and the Christians with salam, and when one of you meets one of them on the road, let him force him to the narrowest part of it."
"7205","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not sell food until you have bought it and taken full possession of it."
"7206","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not sell what you do not have."
"7207","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No necklace of bowstring should remain on the neck of a camel without being cut off."
"7208","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not weep over him; the angels kept shading him with their wings until you lifted him up."
"7209","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not sell one dinar for two dinars, nor one dirham for two dirhams."
"7210","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Sell gold for gold only equal for equal, and silver for silver only equal for equal; and sell gold for silver and silver for gold however you wish."
"7211","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Sell gold for gold only like for like, and do not give one more than the other; sell silver for silver only like for like, and do not give one more than the other; and do not sell any of them that is absent (on credit) for what is present (in hand)."
"7212","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Sell gold for gold only weight for weight."
"7213","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Sell gold for gold and silver for silver only weight for weight, like for like, equal for equal."
"7214","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not acquire estates (land and farms), lest you become attached to this world."
"7215","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not make the mosques into thoroughfares, except for remembrance (of Allah) or prayer."
"7216","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not make your houses into graves."
"7217","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not make your houses into graves; pray in them."
"7218","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not make any living thing a target."
"7219","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This Ummah will not leave any of the ways of the earlier nations without adopting it."
"7220","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not leave fire (burning) in your houses when you go to sleep."
"7221","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not wish for death."
"7222","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not wish to meet the enemy, but when you meet them, stand firm."
"7223","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not dispute about the Qur'an, for disputing about it is disbelief."
"7224","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's prayer does not suffice until he keeps his back straight in bowing and prostration."
"7225","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The prayer in which a man does not keep his back straight in bowing and prostration does not suffice."
"7226","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not make your houses into graves, and do not make my grave a place of festivity. Send blessings upon me, for your blessings reach me wherever you are."
"7227","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not make your houses into graveyards. Indeed, Satan flees from the house in which Surah al-Baqarah is recited."
"7228","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not sit between two men except with their permission."
"7229","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not sit on graves, and do not pray facing them."
"7230","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not combine lying and hunger."
"7231","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not combine my name and my kunyah."
"7232","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not make nabidh by mixing fresh ripe dates with unripe dates, or raisins with dried dates."
"7233","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A mother's crime is not charged against her child."
"7234","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No soul is held responsible for the crime of another."
"7235","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The testimony of a desert-dweller (Bedouin) against a town-dweller is not valid."
"7236","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The testimony of a treacherous man or a treacherous woman is not valid, nor that of a man or woman who commits zina, nor that of one who harbours rancour against his brother in Islam."
"7237","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The testimony of one under suspicion (accused) is not valid, nor that of one who bears a grudge."
"7238","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a woman to give a gift from her wealth without her husband's permission, when her husband holds her marriage bond (that is, when she is married to him)."
"7239","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not stare at those suffering from leprosy."
"7240","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One suck or two sucks (of breast milk) do not establish the prohibition of fosterage."
"7241","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One suck or two sucks do not establish the prohibition of fosterage."
"7242","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not envy one another, do not raise bids deceptively against one another, do not hate one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and let none of you sell over the sale of another. O servants of Allah, be brothers to one another. The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim; he neither forsakes him nor looks down on him. Taqwa (God-consciousness) is here"" - and he (peace and blessings be upon him) pointed to his chest - ""it is enough evil for a person that he looks down on his Muslim brother. For every Muslim, the blood, wealth and honour of another Muslim are sacred (forbidden)."
"7243","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not deliberately aim your prayer at the time of sunrise or sunset, for it rises between the two horns of Satan."
"7244","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not think that we slaughtered this goat because of you. We have a hundred goats and we do not want them to exceed that number, so whenever a young one is born to the shepherd's flock, we slaughter a goat in its place."
"7245","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not look down on any good deed, even if it is meeting your brother with a cheerful face."
"7246","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not swear by your forefathers."
"7247","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not swear by your forefathers. Whoever swears by Allah, let him speak the truth; and whoever has an oath sworn to him by Allah, let him be satisfied; and whoever is not satisfied with (an oath by) Allah has no connection with Allah."
"7248","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not swear by your forefathers, nor by the taghut (false deities)."
"7249","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not swear by your forefathers, by your mothers, or by partners set up with Allah. Swear only by Allah, and swear only when you are truthful."
"7250","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Charity is not lawful for a wealthy person except for five: one who fights in the way of Allah, or one appointed to collect it (zakah), or a debtor, or a man who bought it with his own wealth, or a man who had a poor neighbour to whom charity was given, and the poor man then gave that charity as a gift to the wealthy man."
"7251","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Charity is not lawful for a wealthy person, nor for a strong and able-bodied man."
"7252","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Plunder is not lawful, nor is any beast of prey with fangs lawful, nor is the animal lawful that has been tied up (as a target for shooting)."
"7253","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""She is not lawful for the first husband until the second husband has had intercourse with her."
"7254","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not single out the night of Friday from among the other nights for night prayer (qiyam), and do not single out the day of Friday from among the other days for fasting, unless a fast that one of you regularly keeps happens to fall on that day."
"7255","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not differ among yourselves, for those before you differed and they were destroyed."
"7256","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not differ among yourselves, or your hearts will differ as well."
"7257","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not prefer (in rank) some prophets over others, for on the Day of Resurrection the people will swoon, and I will be the first one for whom the earth is split open. Then I will find Musa (peace be upon him) holding one of the legs of the Throne, and I do not know whether he was among those who swooned, or whether he was credited with his first swoon."
"7258","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not prefer me over Musa (peace be upon him), for on the Day of Resurrection the people will swoon and I will swoon along with them, and I will be the first to regain consciousness. Then I will find Musa (peace be upon him) holding on to the side of the Throne, and I do not know whether he too was among those who swooned and regained consciousness before me, or whether he was among those whom Allah exempted."
"7259","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not frighten yourselves with debt."
"7260","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The angels do not enter a house in which there are statues or pictures."
"7261","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The angels do not enter a house in which there is a picture, unless it is a design made in cloth (embroidered)."
"7262","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or a picture."
"7263","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not enter the ruins of these people who were punished except while weeping. If you are not weeping, then do not go to them, lest the same calamity that befell them befall you."
"7264","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not leave any statue without effacing it, nor any raised grave without levelling it."
"7265","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not call for death and do not wish for it. But if someone must call for it, let him say: 'O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is better for me, and cause me to die when death is better for me.'"
"7266","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not pray against yourselves except for good, for the angels say Amin to what you say."
"7267","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not pray against yourselves, your children, your servants or your wealth, lest your supplication coincide with that hour of acceptance from Allah in which something is asked and it is granted to you."
"7268","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not bury your dead at night unless you are compelled to."
"7269","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not keep staring at those afflicted with leprosy."
"7270","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not slaughter an animal that gives milk."
"7271","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Mention your dead only with good."
"7272","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The world will not come to an end until it passes into the hands of the most contemptible person, son of a contemptible person."
"7273","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The days and nights will not come to an end until a group of my Ummah drinks wine, calling it by a name other than its real name."
"7274","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The days and nights will not come to an end until a man called al-Jahjah comes to rule."
"7275","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The world will not end and pass away until a man from my household comes to rule whose name matches my name."
"7276","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not become disbelievers after me, striking the necks of one another."
"7277","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not become disbelievers after me, striking the necks of one another. And a man is not to be held accountable for the crime of his father, nor for the crime of his brother."
"7278","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the sun sets, do not let your livestock and your children out until the darkness of Isha has passed, for the devils are let loose from sunset until the darkness of Isha has passed."
"7279","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not turn away from (your lineage to) your fathers, for whoever turns away from his father, that is disbelief (kufr)."
"7280","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not raise your eyes to the sky during prayer, lest they be snatched away."
"7281","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not give your property as ruqba. Whoever gives something as ruqba, it will belong to the one to whom it was given."
"7282","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not practise ruqba or umra. Whoever gives something as umra or ruqba, it will belong to his heir when he dies."
"7283","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not ride on saddle-cloths of silk blend (khazz) or on leopard skins."
"7284","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My Ummah will remain upon goodness as long as they hasten to break the fast."
"7285","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My Ummah will remain upon the fitrah (natural way) as long as they do not delay the Maghrib prayer until the stars become crowded together."
"7286","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People will keep being thrown into Hell and it will keep saying: 'Are there any more?' until the Lord of Might places His Foot in it, and then its parts will draw together into one another and it will say: 'Enough, enough! By Your Might and Your Generosity!' And there will remain spare space in Paradise until Allah creates a new creation for it and settles them in the remaining space of Paradise."
"7287","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A group of my Ummah will always remain prevailing upon the truth until the Hour is established."
"7288","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A group of my Ummah will always remain prevailing until the command of Allah comes to them, and they will still be prevailing."
"7289","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A group of my Ummah will always remain prevailing upon the truth; those who forsake them will not harm them, until the command of Allah comes while they are in that state."
"7290","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A group of my Ummah will always remain steadfast upon the command of Allah; those who forsake them or oppose them will not harm them, until the command of Allah comes while they are prevailing over the people."
"7291","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A group of my Ummah will always remain firmly established upon the command of Allah; whoever opposes them will not harm them."
"7292","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A group of my Ummah will always remain aided (by Allah); the desertion of those who desert them will not harm them, until the Hour is established."
"7293","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A group of my Ummah will continue to fight upon the truth, prevailing, until the Day of Resurrection. Then Isa bin Maryam (peace be upon him) will descend, and their leader will say: 'Come, lead us in prayer.' He will say: 'No, some of you are leaders over others, as an honour from Allah to this Ummah.'"
"7294","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A group of my Ummah will continue to fight upon the truth and will prevail over their opponents, until the last of them fights the Masih al-Dajjal."
"7295","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A band of my Ummah will continue to fight upon the truth; those who oppose them will not harm them, until the Hour comes to them while they are in that state."
"7296","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A band of my Ummah will continue to fight upon the command of Allah, prevailing over their enemy; those who oppose them will not harm them, until the Hour comes to them while they are in that state."
"7297","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not declare yourselves pure (righteous); Allah knows best who among you are the righteous. Name her Zaynab."
"7298","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman should not give another woman in marriage, nor should a woman give herself in marriage."
"7299","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The feet of the son of Adam will not move away from before his Lord on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked about five things: about his life, on what he spent it; about his youth, in what he wore it out; about his wealth, from where he earned it and on what he spent it; and how much he acted upon his knowledge."
"7300","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The feet of a servant will not move until he is asked about four things: about his life, on what he spent it; about his knowledge, what he did with it; about his wealth, from where he earned it and on what he spent it; and about his body, in what he wore it out."
"7301","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman should not travel except with a mahram, and no man should enter upon her unless a mahram is with her."
"7302","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman should not travel even the distance of one barid unless she is accompanied by a mahram whom she is forbidden to marry."
"7303","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman should not travel for three days without a mahram."
"7304","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman should not travel a distance of two days unless her husband or a mahram of hers is with her. And there is no fasting on two days: Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha."
"7305","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not travel with the Qur'an, for I fear that the enemy will get hold of it."
"7306","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman should not ask for the divorce of her (religious) sister in order to empty her bowl and marry him herself, for she will only receive what has been decreed for her."
"7307","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not ask people for anything, not even your whip if it falls from you; rather, dismount yourself and pick it up."
"7308","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever you ask me about, until the Day of Resurrection, I will tell you about it."
"7309","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not revile anyone, and do not look down upon any good deed, even if it is only speaking to your brother with a cheerful face; indeed, that too is a good deed. Raise your lower garment to the middle of the shin, and if you are unwilling, then to the ankles. Beware of letting the lower garment hang down, for it is a form of arrogance, and Allah does not love arrogance. And if a man reviles you and taunts you with a fault he knows in you, do not taunt him with a fault you know in him, for its evil consequence will fall upon him alone."
"7310","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not revile my Companions. By the One in whose hand is my soul! If one of you were to spend gold equal to (the mountain of) Uhud, it would not reach a mudd of one of them, nor even half of it."
"7311","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not revile the dead, for they have reached what they sent forth (of deeds)."
"7312","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not revile the dead, for by doing so you hurt the living."
"7313","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not revile time, for Allah is time."
"7314","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not revile the rooster, for it wakes people up for prayer."
"7315","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not revile the wind. When you see something in it that you dislike, say: 'O Allah, we ask You for the good of this wind, the good of what is in it, and the good of what it has been commanded with; and we seek refuge with You from the evil of this wind, the evil of what is in it, and the evil of what it has been commanded with.'"
"7316","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not revile the wind, for it is from the mercy of Allah Almighty; it brings both mercy and punishment. Rather, ask Allah for its good and seek refuge with Allah from its evil."
"7317","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not revile the wind, for it is from the mercy of Allah. Ask Allah for its good, the good of what is in it and the good of what it has been sent with, and seek refuge with Allah from its evil, the evil of what is in it and the evil of what it has been sent with."
"7318","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not revile Satan, and seek refuge with Allah from his evil."
"7319","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not revile Tubba', for he had become a Muslim."
"7320","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not revile Waraqah bin Nawfal, for I have seen one or two gardens of Paradise for him."
"7321","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not revile fever, for it removes the sins of the children of Adam just as the furnace removes the impurities of iron."
"7322","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not revile fever, for it removes sins just as fire removes the impurities of iron."
"7323","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not think that your provision is slow in coming, for no servant dies until the last of the provision decreed for him has reached him. So fear Allah and be moderate in seeking: take what is lawful and leave what is unlawful."
"7324","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not go out of the market to meet the caravan before it reaches the town, do not tie up the udders of animals, and let none of you get a sale made for another by (falsely) raising the bid."
"7325","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not clean yourselves after relieving yourselves (istinja) with dung or bones, for they are the food of your brothers among the jinn."
"7326","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not live in remote villages, for one who lives in such a place is like one who lives in the graves."
"7327","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not give greetings like the greeting of the Jews and the Christians, for their greeting is a gesture with the palms."
"7328","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not name your slave Rabah, Aflah, Yasar or Najih, lest it be asked: 'Is he there?' and the reply be: 'No.'"
"7329","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not name your slave Rabah, Yasar, Aflah or Nafi'."
"7330","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not call grapes 'karm', and do not say 'the failure of time', for Allah is time."
"7331","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not buy it, and do not take back your charity, even if he gives it to you for one dirham, for the one who takes back his charity is like one who licks up his own vomit."
"7332","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Saddles should not be fastened for travel except to three mosques: al-Masjid al-Haram, this mosque of mine, and al-Masjid al-Aqsa."
"7333","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not drink any intoxicant, for I have made every intoxicant unlawful."
"7334","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not drink wine, for it is the key to every evil."
"7335","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not drink from vessels of gold and silver, nor eat from their plates, and do not wear silk or brocade, for these are for them (the disbelievers) in this world and will be for you in the Hereafter."
"7336","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not drink from dubba', muzaffat or naqir, and prepare nabidh in waterskins. If it becomes strong in the waterskins, pour water over it. Indeed, Allah has made wine, gambling and the kubah unlawful, and every intoxicant is unlawful."
"7337","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not drink from naqir, dubba' or hantamah; you must use the waterskin with its mouth tied."
"7338","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not drink from naqir, muzaffat, dubba' or hantam, and drink from the waterskin with its mouth tied. If it becomes strong, break its strength by mixing it with water, and if it still gets the better of you, pour it away."
"7339","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not associate anything with Allah, even if you are cut to pieces or burned; do not deliberately abandon an obligatory prayer, for whoever deliberately abandons it, the protection (of Allah) is withdrawn from him; and do not drink wine, for it is the key to every evil."
"7340","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not tattoo, and do not seek to be tattooed."
"7341","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep company only with a believer, and let only a God-fearing person eat your food."
"7342","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The angels do not accompany a caravan in which there is a bell."
"7343","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The angels do not accompany a caravan in which there are bells."
"7344","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The angels do not accompany a caravan in which there is a dog or a bell."
"7345","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The angels do not accompany a caravan in which there is a leopard skin."
"7346","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Neither affirm the People of the Book nor deny them; rather, say: We believe in Allah and in what has been revealed to us."
"7347","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not tie up the udders of she-camels and goats (to hold back the milk). Whoever buys such an animal in that state has a choice between two options after milking it: if he wishes, he may keep it, and if he wishes, he may return it along with a sa' of dates."
"7348","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not pray facing a grave, nor pray upon a grave."
"7349","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not pray behind a person who is sleeping, nor behind one who is talking."
"7350","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not offer the same prayer twice in one day."
"7351","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not pray in the resting places of camels, for they are of the devils; and pray in the pens of goats, for they are a source of blessing."
"7352","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman should not fast (a voluntary fast) while her husband is present without his permission, other than in Ramadan; and she should not permit anyone to enter his house while he is present without his permission; and whatever she spends from his earnings without his instruction, half of its reward is for him (the husband)."
"7353","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not fast until you see the new moon, and do not stop fasting until you see it; and if it is clouded over for you, then estimate for it."
"7354","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not fast before Ramadan. Fast upon sighting the moon and stop fasting upon sighting it; and if clouds come between you and it, then complete thirty days."
"7355","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not fast on these days, the days of Tashriq, for they are days of eating and drinking."
"7356","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not fast on Friday unless you also fast a day before it or a day after it."
"7357","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not fast on Friday alone."
"7358","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not fast on Saturday except for an obligatory fast; and if any of you finds nothing but a grapevine twig or the bark of a tree, let him break his fast with that."
"7359","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No woman should fast (a voluntary fast) without her husband's permission."
"7360","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not strike the female servants of Allah (women)."
"7361","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not cook in the pots of the polytheists; and if you find nothing other than them, then wash them thoroughly, then cook in them and eat."
"7362","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not come to your women suddenly (without notice) at night."
"7363","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not exaggerate in praising me as the Christians exaggerated in praising the son of Maryam. I am only a servant, so say about me: the servant of Allah and His Messenger."
"7364","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not feed the poor with what you yourselves do not eat."
"7365","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The same prayer should not be repeated twice in one day."
"7366","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not be impressed by the deeds of anyone who does deeds until you see what his end will be."
"7367","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not punish anyone with the punishment of Allah (that is, fire)."
"7368","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not torment your children by pressing (their throats) because of throat inflammation ('udhrah); rather, you must use costus (qust, Indian aloeswood)."
"7369","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In discretionary punishment (ta'zir), do not strike more than ten lashes."
"7370","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not acquire knowledge in order to boast of it before the scholars, or to argue with the foolish by means of it, or to try to stand out in gatherings by means of it. Whoever does that, for him is the Fire, the Fire."
"7371","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Mounts are to be wearied (in travel) only towards three mosques: towards al-Masjid al-Haram, towards this mosque of mine, and towards the mosque of Bayt al-Maqdis."
"7372","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After today, Makkah will never be attacked until the Day of Resurrection."
"7373","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not become angry."
"7374","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not become angry, and Paradise is yours."
"7375","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not let the Bedouins prevail over you concerning the name of your prayer, 'Isha', for in the Book of Allah it is 'Isha', whereas they call it 'Atamah' because they delay (at night) in milking the camels."
"7376","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not let the Bedouins prevail over you concerning the name of your prayer, for it is 'Isha'; they only call it 'Atamah' because of their delaying with the camels."
"7377","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not prefer one of the Prophets of Allah over another, for when the Trumpet is blown, whoever is in the heavens and whoever is on the earth will fall unconscious, except whom Allah wills. Then it will be blown a second time, and I will be the first to be raised. Then I will find Musa (peace be upon him) holding on to the Throne, and I do not know whether he was recompensed for his swoon on the Day of Tur, or whether he was raised before me. And I do not say that anyone is better than Yunus bin Matta."
"7378","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not do that. Sell all (the dates) for dirhams, then with those dirhams buy good-quality dates."
"7379","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not do that, for one of you standing for a while in the path of Allah is better than his praying in his house for seventy years. Do you not wish that Allah should forgive you and admit you into Paradise? Fight in the path of Allah. Whoever fights in the path of Allah even for as long as the interval between two milkings of a she-camel, Paradise becomes obligatory for him."
"7380","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not do as the people of Persia do with their great men."
"7381","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The prescribed punishments (hudud) are not carried out in the mosques, and a father is not executed in retaliation for his son."
"7382","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The prayer of any of you is not accepted when he has become ritually impure, until he performs ablution."
"7383","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The prayer of a woman who has reached puberty is not accepted without a head covering (khimar)."
"7384","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Prayer is not accepted without purification, nor charity given from stolen spoils."
"7385","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The prayer of a woman who puts on perfume to come to this mosque is not accepted until she goes back and bathes in the way the ritual bath for major impurity (janabah) is taken."
"7386","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My heirs shall not divide even a single dinar of mine. Whatever I leave behind, after the maintenance of my wives and the provision of my worker, is charity."
"7387","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No soul is killed unjustly except that a share of its blood is also upon the first son of Adam, because he was the first to establish killing."
"7388","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not kill locusts, for they are of the greatest army of Allah."
"7389","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not kill the house snakes, except every short-tailed one with two stripes, for it causes miscarriage and takes away eyesight; so kill it."
"7390","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not kill frogs."
"7391","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not kill your children secretly. By the One in whose hand is my soul! Ghilah (breastfeeding during pregnancy) overtakes the horseman and knocks him off his horse."
"7392","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not fast a day or two before Ramadan, unless it is a regular fast that one of you observes. Do not fast without seeing the moon, then keep fasting until you see the moon; and if clouds come between you and it, complete thirty days, then stop fasting. And the month may also be of twenty-nine days."
"7393","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not fast a day or two before Ramadan, unless it coincides with someone's regular fast. Fast upon seeing the moon and stop fasting upon seeing the moon; and if clouds cover it over you, count thirty days, then stop fasting."
"7394","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not go ahead of the month until you see the moon or complete the count of the month before it; then keep fasting until you see the moon or complete the count before it."
"7395","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not go ahead of Ramadan by fasting a day or two before it, unless a man has a regular fast, in which case he may observe it."
"7396","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Relate a dream only to a scholar or a sincere well-wisher."
"7397","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hands are not cut off during a journey."
"7398","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The hand is not cut off for hanging dates; but if they have been gathered into the drying-floor, the hand is cut off for theft worth the price of a shield. And the hand is not cut off for an animal grazing unguarded on the mountain; but when it has come into the pen, the hand is cut off for theft worth the price of a shield."
"7399","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The hand of the thief is cut off only for a quarter of a dinar or more."
"7400","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not sit on graves."
"7401","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not say, 'May Satan perish,' for then he grows so big that he becomes as large as a house and says, 'I threw him down by my own strength.' Rather, say, 'Bismillah (In the name of Allah),' for when you say that, he shrinks until he becomes as small as a fly."
"7402","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not say 'Alayka as-salam,' for 'Alayka as-salam' is the greeting of the dead. Rather, say, 'As-salamu 'alayka.'"
"7403","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not say, 'As-salamu 'ala Allah' (Peace be upon Allah), for Allah Himself is As-Salam (Peace). Rather, say: 'At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibat, as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuh, as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin' (All verbal, physical and financial acts of worship are for Allah alone. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah), for when you say this, it reaches every servant in the heavens and the earth. 'Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluh' (I bear witness that there is no true god except Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is His servant and Messenger). Then let him choose whichever supplication he likes and supplicate with it."
"7404","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not say 'al-karm' (for the grapevine); rather, say 'al-'inab' and 'al-habalah'."
"7405","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not call a hypocrite 'our master,' for if he truly is your master, you have angered your Lord."
"7406","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not say, 'What Allah wills and so-and-so wills'; rather, say, 'What Allah wills, then what so-and-so wills.'"
"7407","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will be established only upon the worst of people."
"7408","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until my Ummah adopts the ways of the nations before it, span by span and cubit by cubit."" It was said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Like Persia and Rome?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""And who are the people besides them?"
"7409","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until a fire comes out of the land of the Hijaz that will light up the necks of the camels in Busra."
"7410","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until the buttocks of the women of the tribe of Daws sway around Dhul-Khalasah."
"7411","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until the sun rises from the west. When it rises and the people see it, they will all believe; but that will be the time when faith will not benefit a person who had not believed before or had not earned some good through his faith. And the Hour will be established while two men have spread a garment between them, and they will neither be able to complete its sale nor fold it up. And the Hour will be established while a man has returned with the milk of his she-camel, and he will not be able to drink it. And the Hour will be established while a man is plastering his watering trough, and he will not be able to water his animals from it. And the Hour will be established while a man has raised his morsel to his mouth, and he will not be able to eat it."
"7412","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until the sun rises from the west. When it rises from the west and the people see it, they will all believe; but that will be the time when faith will not benefit a person who had not believed before."
"7413","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until you fight the Turks, whose eyes are small, faces red and noses flat, as if their faces were shields covered with leather. And the Hour will not be established until you fight a people whose sandals are made of hair. And a time will surely come upon one of you when seeing me will be dearer to him than having the like of his family and wealth."
"7414","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until you fight the Jews, until even the stone behind which a Jew is hiding will say: 'O Muslim! There is a Jew behind me, so kill him.'"
"7415","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until you fight Khuz and Kirman from among the non-Arabs, whose faces are red, noses flat and eyes small, as if their faces were shields covered with leather, and whose sandals are made of hair."
"7416","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until you fight a people with small eyes and broad faces, as if their eyes were like the eyes of locusts and their faces like shields covered with leather. They will wear sandals of hair and use small shields, until they tie their horses to the date palms."
"7417","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until two great groups fight each other whose claim is one and the same. And the Hour will not be established until nearly thirty lying Dajjals appear, each of them claiming that he is the Messenger of Allah."
"7418","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until some tribes of my Ummah join the polytheists and until idols are worshipped. And indeed, there will be thirty liars in my Ummah, each of them claiming that he is a prophet, whereas I am Khatam an-Nabiyyin (the Seal of the Prophets); there is no prophet after me."
"7419","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until the Hajj to the House of Allah ceases."
"7420","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until 'Allah, Allah' is no longer said on the earth."
"7421","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until people vie with one another in boasting about the adornment of mosques."
"7422","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until time draws close together: a year will be like a month, a month like a week, a week like a day, a day like an hour, and an hour will be as short as the flaring up of a fire."
"7423","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until the Euphrates uncovers a mountain of gold. People will fight over it, and out of every hundred, ninety-nine will be killed, and every man among them will say: 'Perhaps I will be the one who survives.'"
"7424","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until the Euphrates uncovers a mountain of gold. People will fight over it, and nine-tenths of them will be killed."
"7425","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until a man from Qahtan appears who will drive the people with his staff."
"7426","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until the Muslims fight the Turks, a people whose faces are like shields covered with leather; they will wear hair and walk in hair."
"7427","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until the Muslims fight the Jews and the Muslims kill them, until a Jew will hide behind a stone or a tree, and the stone or tree will say: 'O Muslim! O servant of Allah! There is a Jew behind me, so come and kill him,' except the gharqad tree, for it is one of the trees of the Jews."
"7428","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until knowledge is taken away, earthquakes become frequent, time draws close together, trials appear, and 'harj', that is, killing and bloodshed, becomes widespread."
"7429","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until wealth becomes abundant and overflowing, so much so that a man will go out with the zakah of his wealth and will not find anyone to accept it from him, and until the land of the Arabs becomes pastures and rivers once again."
"7430","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until wealth becomes abundant and overflowing among you, so much so that the owner of wealth will be worried about who will accept his charity, and he will offer it, and the one to whom it is offered will say: 'I have no need of it.'"
"7431","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until the most fortunate person in the world is a base man, son of a base man."
"7432","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until a man passes by the grave of another man and says: 'Would that I were in his place.'"
"7433","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until the Romans land at al-A'maq or at Dabiq. Then an army from Madinah, the best of the people of the earth at that time, will go out to them. When they line up in ranks, the Romans will say: 'Leave us to those of ours who were taken captive from among us; we will fight them.' The Muslims will say: 'No, by Allah! We will not stand aside between you and our brothers.' So they will fight them. A third will be defeated and flee, and Allah will never accept their repentance; a third will be killed, and they will be the most excellent of martyrs in the sight of Allah; and a third will be victorious, and they will never be put to trial. Then they will conquer Constantinople. While they are dividing the spoils, having hung their swords on the olive trees, Satan will suddenly cry out among them: 'The Masih ad-Dajjal has taken your place among your families behind you!' So they will set out, though it will be a lie. Then when they reach Syria, he will appear. While they are preparing for battle and straightening the ranks, the prayer will be called, and Isa bin Maryam (peace be upon him) will descend and lead them in prayer. When the enemy of Allah sees him, he will begin to dissolve as salt dissolves in water; and even if he were left alone, he would go on dissolving until he perished. But Allah will have him killed by the hand of Isa (peace be upon him), and he will show them his blood on his spear."
"7434","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not write anything from me except the Qur'an. Whoever has written anything from me other than the Qur'an, let him erase it. And narrate from me, there is no harm in that. And whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in Hell."
"7435","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not laugh too much, for excessive laughter kills the heart."
"7436","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not lie about me, for lying leads into the Fire."
"7437","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not lie about me, for whoever lies about me, let him enter the Fire."
"7438","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not rent out land."
"7439","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not force your sick ones to eat and drink, for Allah Himself feeds them and gives them drink."
"7440","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not uncover your thigh, and do not look at the thigh of anyone, living or dead."
"7441","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not go to excessive trouble for a guest."
"7442","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not be helpers of Satan against your brother."
"7443","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not curse one another with the curse of Allah, nor with His wrath, nor with the Fire."
"7444","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not wear silk, for whoever wears it in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter."
"7445","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not wear shirts, turbans, trousers, hooded cloaks or leather socks, except for one who cannot find sandals; he may wear leather socks, but let him cut them below the ankles. And do not wear any garment touched by saffron or wars. And the woman in ihram should not wear a face veil or gloves."
"7446","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not be persistent in asking, for by Allah, whoever among you asks me for something and his asking extracts something from me while I am averse to it, he will not be blessed in what I give him."
"7447","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not curse the wind, for it is under command; and whoever curses something that does not deserve it, the curse returns upon him."
"7448","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not go out to meet the trade caravans coming from outside on the road before they reach the town. Whoever does so and buys something from them, the owner of the goods has the option to cancel the sale when he reaches the market."
"7449","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not go out on the road to meet riders to buy from them; none of you should sell over the sale of another; do not raise the bidding deceptively; a town-dweller should not sell for a desert-dweller; and do not tie up the udders of sheep and goats to hold back the milk. Whoever buys such an animal has the choice after milking it: if he is pleased with it, he may keep it, and if he is displeased with it, he may return it along with a sa' of dates."
"7450","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not go out on the road to meet riders, and a town-dweller should not sell for a desert-dweller."
"7451","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not mutilate animals."
"7452","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not wipe away (the pebbles of the ground) while you are praying; and if you must do so, then do it only once, that is, to level the pebbles."
"7453","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not walk in one sandal, do not sit with your knees drawn up and wrapped in a single garment, do not eat with your left hand, do not wrap yourself in a single garment in such a way that there is no opening to bring your hands out, and when you lie on your back, do not place one of your legs over the other."
"7454","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not prevent women from their share of the mosques when they ask your permission."
"7455","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from praying in the mosque."
"7456","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques of Allah."
"7457","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques of Allah, but let them go out without wearing perfume."
"7458","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not prevent your women from the mosques, though their houses are better for them."
"7459","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not soak dry dates and unripe dates together to make nabidh; rather, soak each of them separately."
"7460","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not make nabidh in dubba' (gourd vessels) or muzaffat (pitch-coated vessels)."
"7461","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not soak yellowing unripe dates and fresh ripe dates together to make nabidh, and do not soak dry dates and raisins together either; rather, soak each of them separately."
"7462","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not make nabidh in dubba', muzaffat or naqir, and every intoxicant is unlawful."
"7463","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not pluck out grey hairs. No Muslim grows a grey hair in Islam but that it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"7464","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Armies will not stop attacking this House (the Ka'bah) until an army among them is swallowed up by the earth."
"7465","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People will not stop attacking this House until an army attacks it, and when they reach al-Bayda', or a plain of the earth, the first and last of them will be swallowed up by the earth, and the middle of them will not escape either."" It was said: ""What if there is someone among them who dislikes this?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah will raise them according to their intentions."
"7466","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not make vows, for a vow does not change anything of divine decree; it is only a means by which wealth is extracted from the miser."
"7467","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Mercy is taken away only from a wretched person."
"7468","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not camp on the roads, and do not relieve yourselves on them."
"7469","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Emigration (hijrah) will not come to an end until repentance comes to an end, and repentance will not come to an end until the sun rises from its place of setting."
"7470","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A widow is not to be married until she is consulted, and a virgin is not to be married until her permission is sought."" It was said: ""How will her permission be known?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By her remaining silent."
"7471","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A previously married (widowed or divorced) woman is not to be married until she is consulted, and a virgin is not to be married until her permission is sought, and her permission is her silence."
"7472","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A paternal aunt is not to be combined in marriage with her brother's daughter, nor a sister's daughter with her maternal aunt."
"7473","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman is not to be combined in marriage with her paternal aunt, nor a paternal aunt with her brother's daughter, nor a woman with her maternal aunt, nor a maternal aunt with her sister's daughter; neither the elder with the younger, nor the younger with the elder."
"7474","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman is not to be combined in marriage with her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt."
"7475","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not cut severely, for that is more pleasing for the woman and more beloved to the husband."
"7476","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not observe wisal (continuous fasting without breaking the fast). I am not like any of you; I am given food and drink."
"7477","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not observe wisal; but whoever among you wishes to observe wisal, let him do so until the time of suhur. I am not like you; I spend the night with One who feeds me and One who gives me drink."
"7478","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not join one prayer to another in such a way that you do not speak in between or leave your place."
"7479","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A pregnant woman is not to be had intercourse with until she gives birth, nor one who is not pregnant until she has had a menstrual period."
"7480","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not hold back your wealth, or Allah too will hold back His bounty from you; keep spending as much as you can."
"7481","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not tie up your wealth, or the knot of Allah's mercy will be tied against you too."
"7482","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not stop speaking to one another, do not turn your backs on one another, do not spy on one another, and none of you should sell over the sale of another. And, O servants of Allah, be brothers to one another."
"7483","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In a race there is neither 'jalab' nor 'janab'."
"7484","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is neither 'jalab' nor 'janab', and their zakah is not to be collected anywhere other than at their homes."
"7485","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In Islam there is neither 'jalab', nor 'janab', nor 'shighar'."
"7486","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In Islam there is neither 'jalab', nor 'janab', nor 'shighar'; and whoever plunders is not one of us."
"7487","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Envy (i.e., emulation) is permissible only regarding two people: a man to whom Allah has given the Qur'an and he stands with it in prayer during the hours of the night and the day, and a man to whom Allah has given wealth and he spends it during the hours of the night and the day."
"7488","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Envy is permissible only regarding two people: a man to whom Allah has given wealth and granted him the ability to spend it in the right way, and a man to whom Allah has given wisdom and he judges by it and teaches it."
"7489","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Envy is permissible only regarding two people: a man whom Allah has taught the Qur'an and he recites it during the hours of the night and the day; his neighbour hears him and says: 'If only I were given what so-and-so has been given, I would act as he acts.' And a man to whom Allah has given wealth and he spends it in the right way, and a man says: 'If only I were given what so-and-so has been given, I would act as he acts.'"
"7490","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no new alliance in Islam, and whatever alliance existed in the Jahiliyyah, Islam has only made it stronger."
"7491","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No pasture may be reserved except for Allah and His Messenger."
"7492","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no good in one who does not show hospitality."
"7493","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no false claim of lineage in Islam; the affair of the Jahiliyyah is gone. The child belongs to the owner of the bed (the husband), and for the adulterer is the stone."
"7494","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no usury (riba) in what is exchanged hand to hand (on the spot)."
"7495","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The prohibition of fosterage is established only by the suckling that opens the intestines."
"7496","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ruqyah is done only for the evil eye, a sting, or blood (flowing uncontrollably)."
"7497","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no zakah on wealth until a year has passed over it."
"7498","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A prize for racing is permissible only in a contest of camels, horses, or archery."
"7499","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Staying awake at night for conversation is not permissible, except for one who prays or a traveller."
"7500","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Evil omens have no reality; however, blessing may be in a house, a woman, and a horse."
"7501","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no 'Shighar' marriage in Islam."
"7502","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one has more ghayrah (protective jealousy) than Allah Almighty."
"7503","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The evil eye is real, and the truest of omens is the fa'l (good omen)."
"7504","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Selling two sa' of dates for one sa', two sa' of wheat for one sa', and two dirhams for one dirham is not permissible."
"7505","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Selling two sa' for one sa' and two dirhams for one dirham is not permissible."
"7506","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts perpetually (every day) has not truly fasted."
"7507","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts perpetually has not truly fasted. Fasting three days is equal to fasting the whole of time."
"7508","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no fasting above the fasting of Dawud (peace be upon him), that is, fasting half of time: fast one day and break the fast one day."
"7509","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Prayer should not be offered when food is present, nor in the state when one is holding back the call of urine or stool."
"7510","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no prayer after Fajr until the sun has risen high, and there is no prayer after Asr until the sun has set."
"7511","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no prayer after Fajr except two rak'ahs."
"7512","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not recite Umm al-Qur'an or more, his prayer is not valid."
"7513","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not recite Fatihat al-Kitab, his prayer is not valid."
"7514","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no prayer for one who has no ablution, and there is no ablution for one who did not mention the name of Allah over it."
"7515","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no prayer for one who has no ablution, and there is no ablution for one who did not mention the name of Allah over it."
"7516","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever did not make the intention to fast from the night before, there is no fast for him."
"7517","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not cause harm, and do not retaliate by causing harm."
"7518","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no liability (for loss) upon one who is entrusted."
"7519","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no obedience to anyone in disobedience to Allah; obedience is only in what is good."
"7520","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no obedience to any creature in disobedience to the Creator."
"7521","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no obedience to one who does not obey Allah."
"7522","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Divorce takes effect only in what one owns, freeing a slave takes effect only in what one owns, a sale takes effect only in what one owns, fulfilling a vow applies only in what one owns, and a vow is valid only when the pleasure of Allah is sought by it. Whoever swears an oath to commit a sin, his oath has no standing, and whoever swears an oath to sever ties of kinship, his oath too has no standing."
"7523","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Divorce does not take effect before marriage."
"7524","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no divorce before marriage and no freeing of a slave before ownership."
"7525","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Neither divorce nor freeing of a slave takes effect in a state of coercion."
"7526","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Evil omens have no reality, and the best form of it is the 'fa'l': a good word that one of you hears."
"7527","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Contagion spreading of its own accord, Safar, and Hamah have no reality."
"7528","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Contagion spreading of its own accord and evil omens have no reality; however, ill fortune may be in three things: in a horse, a woman, and a house."
"7529","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Contagion spreading of its own accord, evil omens, and Hamah have no reality. So who gave the mange to the first one?"
"7530","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Contagion spreading of its own accord, evil omens, Hamah, and Safar have no reality, and flee from the leper as you flee from a lion."
"7531","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Contagion spreading of its own accord, evil omens, Hamah, Safar, and Ghul have no reality."
"7532","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Contagion spreading of its own accord and evil omens have no reality, and I like a good omen, and what is meant by a good omen is a good word."
"7533","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Contagion spreading of its own accord, Hamah, and evil omens have no reality, and I like a good omen."
"7534","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Contagion spreading of its own accord, Hamah, Naw', and Safar have no reality."
"7535","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no 'aqr (the custom of slaughtering animals at a grave) in Islam."
"7536","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No punishment may exceed ten lashes, except in one of the prescribed punishments (hudud) of Allah."
"7537","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no harm upon you if you do not do it, for Allah Almighty has already written whatever He is to create until the Day of Resurrection."
"7538","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no harm upon you if you do not do it. Whatever Allah has written to create, every soul that is to come into existence until the Day of Resurrection will certainly come into existence."
"7539","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The condition of 'umra is not valid; whoever gives something as 'umra, it becomes his (the recipient's)."
"7540","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The conditions of 'umra and ruqba are not valid; whoever gives something as 'umra or ruqba, it becomes his, both in his life and after his death."
"7541","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is to be no deficiency in the prayer, nor in the salam."
"7542","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Usurpation and plunder are not permissible."
"7543","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ghouls have no reality."
"7544","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The customs of Far' and 'Atirah are not part of Islam."
"7545","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The hand is not cut off for the theft of fruit, nor of the pith of the date palm."
"7546","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A vow is not valid in disobedience to Allah, nor in something that the son of Adam does not own."
"7547","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A vow to do a sinful act is not valid, and its expiation is like the expiation for an oath."
"7548","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The vow of the son of Adam is not valid regarding what he does not own, his oath is not valid regarding what he does not own, and his divorce does not take effect regarding what he does not own."
"7549","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The vow and oath of the son of Adam are not valid in what he does not own, nor in disobedience to Allah, nor in severing ties of kinship."
"7550","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no maintenance for you unless you are pregnant."
"7551","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is neither maintenance nor housing for you."
"7552","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The additional award (nafl) is given only after the one-fifth (khumus) has been taken out."
"7553","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We do not cross the valley of Abtah except at a run."
"7554","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We do not cross the valley except at a run."
"7555","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no marriage without a guardian (wali)."
"7556","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no marriage without a guardian, and the ruler is the guardian of the one who has no guardian."
"7557","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no marriage without a guardian and two upright witnesses."
"7558","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no marriage without a guardian and two witnesses."
"7559","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We Prophets are not inherited from; whatever we leave behind is charity."
"7560","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We Prophets are not inherited from; whatever we leave behind is charity. The family of Muhammad only eat from this wealth."
"7561","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We Prophets are not inherited from; whatever we leave behind is charity. This wealth is only for the needs of the family of Muhammad and for their hospitality to guests. So when I die, it will pass to the one in authority after me."
"7562","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hamah, the self-transmission of disease, and bad omens have no reality. And if a bad omen could be in anything, it would be in a horse, a woman and a house."
"7563","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no emigration (hijrah) after the Conquest, but jihad and intention remain. And when you are called to go forth, then go forth."
"7564","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Cutting off relations for more than three days is not permissible."
"7565","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no emigration (hijrah) after the Conquest of Makkah."
"7566","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no emigration (hijrah), but jihad and intention remain. And when you are called to go forth, then go forth. Indeed, Allah made this city (Makkah) sacred on the day He created the heavens and the earth, and it is sacred by the sanctity of Allah until the Day of Resurrection. Fighting in it was not made lawful for anyone before me, nor was it made lawful for me except for an hour of a day. So it is sacred by the sanctity of Allah until the Day of Resurrection: its thorns are not to be cut, its game is not to be startled, its lost property is not to be picked up by anyone except one who announces it, and its fresh grass is not to be cut, except the idhkhir."
"7567","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are no two witr prayers in one night."
"7568","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May you not find it! May you not find it! May you not find it! These mosques were built only for the purpose for which they were built."
"7569","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no continuous fasting (wisal) in fasting."
"7570","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A bequest for an heir is not permissible."
"7571","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ablution (wudu) is broken only by passing wind or hearing its sound."
"7572","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ablution (wudu) is broken only by a sound or by passing wind."
"7573","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no ablution (wudu) for the one who did not mention the name of Allah over it."
"7574","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible to fulfil a vow based on disobedience to Allah."
"7575","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever comes to his master and asks him for some surplus that he has, and he refuses to give it to him, on the Day of Resurrection a bald snake will be brought for him, licking its lips, because of the surplus that he withheld."
"7576","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No year or day will come upon you except that the one after it will be worse than it, until you meet your Lord."
"7577","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever takes even a handspan of land unjustly, Allah will make him wear it as a collar down to seven earths on the Day of Resurrection."
"7578","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should take his companion's belongings, whether in jest or in earnest. And if someone has taken his companion's staff, he should return it to him."
"7579","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should eat with his left hand nor drink with his left hand, for Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand."
"7580","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should eat the meat of his sacrificial animal beyond three days."
"7581","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No man should lead another in prayer within his authority without his permission, nor sit in his special seat in his house without his permission."
"7582","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you truly believes until I am more beloved to him than his children, his father and all people."
"7583","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you truly believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself."
"7584","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A servant does not truly believe until he believes in four things: that he bears witness to 'La ilaha illallah' (there is no true god except Allah) and that I am the Messenger of Allah, whom He sent with the truth; that he believes in death; that he believes in the resurrection after death; and that he believes in divine decree, its good and its evil."
"7585","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A servant does not truly believe until he believes in divine decree, its good and its evil, until he is certain that whatever reached him could not have missed him, and whatever missed him could not have reached him."
"7586","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Surplus water is not to be sold in order that the use of the pasture be sold through it."
"7587","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should make a sale over the sale of his brother."
"7588","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man should not make a sale over the sale of his brother until he buys or leaves it."
"7589","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should make a sale over the sale of another, and do not go out to meet the trade goods on the way until they are brought down to the market."
"7590","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should make a sale over the sale of another, nor should any of you propose marriage over the proposal of another."
"7591","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A town-dweller should not sell for a desert-dweller; do not inflate bids deceitfully; a man should not make a sale over his brother's sale, nor propose marriage over his brother's proposal; and a woman should not ask for her sister's divorce so as to empty her bowl and marry herself, for she will receive only what Allah has decreed for her."
"7592","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A person who believes in Allah and the Last Day does not bear hatred toward the Ansar."
"7593","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should urinate in stagnant water, which does not flow, and then bathe in it."
"7594","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should urinate in stagnant water and then perform ablution (wudu) from it."
"7595","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should urinate in stagnant water, nor take the ritual bath (ghusl) for janabah in it."
"7596","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should urinate in stagnant water."
"7597","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should urinate in his bathing place."
"7598","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should urinate while facing the Qiblah."
"7599","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No man should spend the night with a woman in a house unless he is her husband or a mahram."
"7600","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man should not make a sale over his brother's sale, nor propose marriage over his brother's proposal, unless he gives him permission."
"7601","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man should not make a sale over his brother's sale, nor bid over his brother's bid."
"7602","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A town-dweller should not sell for a desert-dweller."
"7603","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A town-dweller should not sell for a desert-dweller. Leave people alone; Allah provides for some of them through others."
"7604","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People should sit together in a gathering only when trust (confidentiality) is observed."
"7605","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let people not say that Muhammad has his companions killed."
"7606","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should deliberately aim to pray at the time of sunrise or sunset."
"7607","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Those who make a transaction should not part except with mutual consent."
"7608","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one should burden himself for his guest with what he cannot afford."
"7609","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no orphanhood after reaching puberty (ihtilam), nor is it permissible to remain silent for a day until night."
"7610","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should wish for death. If he is a doer of good, perhaps he will increase in good; and if he is a wrongdoer, perhaps he will repent and seek to earn (Allah's) pleasure."
"7611","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should wish for death because of some hardship that has befallen him. If he must wish, then let him say: 'Allahumma ahyini ma kanat al-hayatu khayran li, wa tawaffani idha kanat al-wafatu khayran li' (O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is better for me, and cause me to die when death is better for me)."
"7612","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should wish for death, nor call for it before it comes to him, for when one of you dies his deeds come to an end, and the life of a believer only increases him in good."
"7613","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of two different religions do not inherit from one another."
"7614","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of two separate religions do not inherit from one another."
"7615","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs ablution (wudu) well and then prays, his sins between that and the following prayer are forgiven."
"7616","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Dust in the path of Allah and the smoke of Hell can never come together in the belly of a servant, and miserliness and faith can never come together in the heart of a servant."
"7617","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Dust in the path of Allah and the smoke of Hell can never come together in the nostrils of a Muslim."
"7618","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A disbeliever and the one who killed him will never be together in Hell."
"7619","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two people will not be gathered together in Hell in such a way that one harms the other: a believer who killed a disbeliever and then remained steadfast in the religion."
"7620","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A Muslim who killed a disbeliever and then remained steadfast and kept to moderation will not be gathered together with him in Hell; dust in the path of Allah and the heat of Hell cannot come together in the belly of a believer; and faith and envy cannot come together in the heart of a servant."
"7621","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman should not be combined (in marriage) with her paternal aunt, nor with her maternal aunt."
"7622","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A child cannot repay the right of his father, unless he finds him a slave and buys him and sets him free."
"7623","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one is flogged more than ten lashes except in one of the prescribed punishments (hudud) of Allah."
"7624","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No people should sit in a gathering in which they do not send blessings upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), otherwise it will be a cause of regret for them, even if they enter Paradise, because of the reward they will see."
"7625","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a woman to dispose freely of her wealth while her husband holds her marital bond."
"7626","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman's gift is not permissible unless her husband permits it."
"7627","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The members of a household that has dates will not go hungry."
"7628","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None keeps up the Duha (forenoon) prayer except one who constantly turns to Allah, and it is the prayer of the Awwabin (those who constantly turn to Allah)."
"7629","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None loves the Ansar except a believer, and none hates them except a hypocrite. Whoever loves them, Allah loves him, and whoever hates them, Allah hates him."
"7630","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah does not like disobedience. Whoever has a child born to him and wishes to offer a sacrifice (aqiqah) on its behalf, let him slaughter two sheep of equal age for a boy and one sheep for a girl."
"7631","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None hoards except a sinner."
"7632","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After this year no polytheist shall perform Hajj, and no one shall circumambulate the House (Ka'bah) naked."
"7633","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The prohibition (of marriage) through breastfeeding is established only by suckling that opens the intestines and takes place before weaning."
"7634","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should belittle any good deed. If he finds nothing (else), let him meet his brother with a cheerful face. And when you buy meat or cook a pot, add more broth to it and give some of it to your neighbour as well."
"7635","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should judge between two people while he is angry."
"7636","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one should milk another person's livestock without his permission. Would any of you like to have his storeroom entered, its lock broken and his food taken away?! Indeed, the udders of their livestock are the stores of their food, so no one should milk anyone's livestock without his permission."
"7637","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one should swear a false oath near my pulpit, even over a fresh tooth-stick (miswak), otherwise Hell will become obligatory for him."
"7638","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one should swear a false oath near this pulpit of mine, even over a green tooth-stick (miswak), otherwise he will take his seat in Hell."
"7639","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for the freed slave of a Muslim man to take someone else as his patron (wala') without his permission."
"7640","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The price of a dog, the fee of a soothsayer and the earnings of a prostitute are not lawful."
"7641","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except for one of three reasons: a man who commits adultery after being married, or who apostatises after accepting Islam, or who kills a soul unjustly, so he is killed in retaliation for it."
"7642","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The blood of a Muslim who bears witness to 'La ilaha illallah wa anna Muhammadan rasulullah' (There is no true god except Allah, and Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah) is not lawful except for one of three reasons: a man who commits adultery after being married, so he is to be stoned; a man who goes out waging war against Allah and His Messenger, so he is to be killed, or crucified, or exiled from the land; or one who kills a soul, so he is killed in retaliation for it."
"7643","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The blood of a Muslim who bears witness to 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no true god except Allah) and that I am the Messenger of Allah is not lawful except for one of three reasons: the married adulterer, a life for a life, and the one who abandons his religion and separates from the community."
"7644","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible to combine a loan and a sale, nor to set two conditions in one sale, nor to take profit on something that is not under your liability, nor to sell what you do not have."
"7645","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for any of you to carry weapons in Makkah."
"7646","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a woman to travel unless she has a mahram with her."
"7647","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a woman to fast while her husband is present without his permission, nor to permit anyone to enter his house without his permission. And whatever she spends without his instruction, half of its reward will be given to him."
"7648","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn for a deceased person for more than three nights, except for a husband, for whom she mourns four months and ten days."
"7649","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn for more than three days, except for a husband, for whom she mourns four months and ten days. During this time she should not apply kohl, nor wear dyed clothes except a striped garment, nor use perfume, except that when she becomes pure from her menstruation she may use a little qust or azfar."
"7650","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to undertake a journey of three days or more unless her father, her son, her husband, her brother or some other mahram is with her."
"7651","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel a distance of three days unless a mahram is with her."
"7652","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel a distance of one day except with a mahram."
"7653","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel a distance of a day and a night except with a mahram."
"7654","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a man who believes in Allah and the Last Day to water another person's crops with his water, nor to buy spoils of war before they are distributed, nor to wear a garment from the fay' of the Muslims such that when it has worn out he returns it, nor to ride an animal from the fay' of the Muslims such that when it has become emaciated he returns it."
"7655","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a man to give a gift or a present and then take it back, except a father regarding what he gives his child. The example of one who gives a gift and then takes it back is like a dog that eats, and when it is full it vomits, then goes back to lick its vomit."
"7656","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a man to separate two people without their permission."
"7657","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a believer to cut off relations with his brother for more than three days."
"7658","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a Muslim to frighten a Muslim."
"7659","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a Muslim to cut off relations with his brother for more than three days. Whoever cuts off relations for more than three days and dies in that state will enter Hell."
"7660","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a Muslim to cut off relations with his brother for more than three nights, such that when they meet, this one turns away and that one turns away. The better of the two is the one who initiates the greeting of salam."
"7661","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Not even something as trivial as this from your spoils of war is lawful for me, except the one-fifth (khums), and even the one-fifth is returned to you."
"7662","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The wealth of a Muslim is not lawful without his heartfelt consent."
"7663","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let nothing trouble your heart in which you have imitated Christianity."
"7664","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should propose marriage over the proposal of his brother."
"7665","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should propose marriage over the proposal of his brother until he marries or withdraws."
"7666","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man should not propose marriage over the proposal of his brother, nor bid over the bid of his brother; a woman should not be married together with her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt; and a woman should not ask for her sister's divorce in order to empty her bowl and marry him herself, for she will only get what Allah has decreed for her."
"7667","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you will be admitted into Paradise by his deeds, nor will they save him from Hell, nor me either, except through the mercy of Allah."
"7668","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one will enter Paradise without being shown the place he would have had in Hell had he done evil, so that his gratitude may increase; and no one will enter Hell without being shown the place he would have had in Paradise had he done good, so that it may become a source of regret for him."
"7669","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The jawwaz (the harsh-tempered miser) and the ja'zari (the one who struts about arrogantly) will not enter Paradise."
"7670","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None will enter Paradise except a Muslim soul; no one will circumambulate the House naked; after this year of theirs, Muslims and polytheists will not gather together in al-Masjid al-Haram; whoever has a covenant with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), his covenant stands until its term; and whoever has no covenant, his respite is four months."
"7671","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who severs ties of kinship will not enter Paradise."
"7672","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The talebearer will not enter Paradise."
"7673","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The habitual drinker of wine will not enter Paradise."
"7674","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has an atom's weight of arrogance in his heart will not enter Paradise. It was said: A man likes his garment to be fine and his sandals to be fine. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah is beautiful and loves beauty; arrogance is rejecting the truth and looking down on people."
"7675","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He whose neighbour is not safe from his harm will not enter Paradise."
"7676","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who reminds others of his favours, the one who is disobedient to his parents, and the habitual drinker of wine will not enter Paradise."
"7677","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Masih ad-Dajjal and the plague will not enter Madinah."
"7678","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The terror of the Masih ad-Dajjal will not enter Madinah. On that day Madinah will have seven gates, and at every gate there will be two angels."
"7679","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one who has a mustard seed's weight of faith in his heart will enter Hell, and no one who has a mustard seed's weight of arrogance in his heart will enter Paradise."
"7680","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of those who gave the pledge of allegiance under the tree will enter Hell."
"7681","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After this day of mine, no man should enter upon a woman whose husband is absent unless one or two other men are with him."
"7682","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should slaughter his sacrifice before offering the (Eid) prayer."
"7683","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Night and day will not come to an end until al-Lat and al-Uzza are worshipped again. Then Allah Almighty will send a pleasant wind that will take the soul of everyone who has a mustard seed's weight of faith in his heart, so only those in whom there is no good will remain, and they will return to the religion of their forefathers."
"7684","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Night and day will not come to an end until a man from among the freed slaves, called Jahjah, becomes a ruler."
"7685","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The disbeliever does not inherit from the Muslim, nor does the Muslim inherit from the disbeliever."
"7686","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one may take back his gift (hibah), except a father, who may take back what he has given his child. The one who takes back his gift is like one who eats his vomit again."
"7687","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Nothing averts destiny except supplication, and nothing increases one's lifespan except righteousness."
"7688","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One of you continues to be (counted as in prayer) as long as the prayer keeps him waiting, and nothing prevents him from returning to his family except the prayer."
"7689","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The religion will remain dominant as long as people hasten to break their fast, because the Jews and Christians delay (breaking their fast)."
"7690","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The servant continues to be (counted as in prayer) as long as he is in the mosque waiting for the prayer, so long as he does not lose his ablution."
"7691","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A servant remains in latitude in his religion as long as he does not shed unlawful blood."
"7692","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty will continue to raise up people in this religion whom He will keep engaged in His obedience until the Day of Resurrection."
"7693","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believer continues to hasten forward in righteousness as long as he does not shed unlawful blood; then when he sheds unlawful blood, he becomes exhausted and comes to a halt (on the path of righteousness)."
"7694","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People will remain upon good as long as they hasten to break the fast."
"7695","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People will remain upon good as long as they hasten to break the fast, for the Jews break their fast late."
"7696","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People will keep questioning one another until it is said: Allah created all this creation, so who created Allah? So whoever finds any such thought within himself, let him say: I believe in Allah and His Messenger."
"7697","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of the West will remain prevailing upon the truth until the Hour is established."
"7698","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The heart of an old man remains young in two things: in love of the world and in long hopes."
"7699","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people will keep holding back from the first row (of prayer) until Allah holds them back in the Fire."
"7700","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May your tongue always remain moist with the remembrance of Allah."
"7701","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people from my Ummah will always remain prevailing upon the truth until the command of Allah (the Hour) comes to them while they are still prevailing."
"7702","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This matter (the caliphate) will remain among Quraysh as long as even two people remain in the world."
"7703","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This religion will remain established until twelve caliphs have ruled over you, upon each of whom the whole Ummah will agree, all of them from Quraysh; then there will be killing and turmoil."
"7704","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This religion will remain established, with a group of the Muslims fighting for it, until the Hour is established."
"7705","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The supplication of a servant will continue to be answered as long as he does not pray for something sinful or for severing ties of kinship, and as long as he is not hasty, (that is,) he says: I prayed and I prayed but my prayer was not answered, and then he becomes despondent over that and abandons supplication."
"7706","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The adulterer is not a believer at the time he commits adultery, the thief is not a believer at the time he steals, and the drinker is not a believer at the time he drinks wine; and after that, the door of repentance remains open."
"7707","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The adulterer is not a believer at the time he commits adultery, the drinker is not a believer at the time he drinks wine, the thief is not a believer at the time he steals, and when a person plunders something valuable in such a way that people raise their eyes to look at him, he is not a believer at that time."
"7708","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A servant is not a believer at the time he commits adultery, he is not a believer at the time he steals, he is not a believer at the time he drinks wine, and he is not a believer at the time he kills."
"7709","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is asked by his master for surplus wealth that he has, and he withholds it from him, then on the Day of Resurrection that surplus wealth of his which he withheld will be brought in the form of a bald serpent."
"7710","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should revile time, for Allah is time (its Creator and Master); and none of you should call the grape karm, for karm (the noble one) is the Muslim man."
"7711","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah is not shy of stating the truth, Allah is not shy of stating the truth: do not approach women in their backsides (anus)."
"7712","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever servant Allah Almighty conceals (the faults of) in this world, He will also conceal on the Day of Resurrection."
"7713","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever servant conceals (the faults of) another servant in this world, Allah will conceal him on the Day of Resurrection."
"7714","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A person should not lie on his back and place one of his legs over the other."
"7715","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should cleanse himself after relieving himself (istinja) with fewer than three stones."
"7716","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should point a weapon at his brother, for he does not know; perhaps Satan may (jerk) his hand and he may fall into a pit of the Fire."
"7717","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever a man of my Ummah drinks wine, Allah does not accept his prayer for forty days."
"7718","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should drink while standing."
"7719","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not thank people does not thank Allah."
"7720","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever testifies that La ilaha illallah (there is no god worthy of worship except Allah) and that I am the Messenger of Allah will not enter the Fire, nor will the Fire consume him."
"7721","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever of my Ummah bears patiently the hardship and difficulty of Madinah, I will be an intercessor or a witness for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"7722","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting is not proper on two days: the day of Eid al-Adha and the day of Eid al-Fitr after Ramadan."
"7723","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Lying is permissible only on three occasions: a man speaking to his wife to please her, lying in war, and lying to make peace between people."
"7724","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One sa' of dates for two sa's is not proper, nor one dirham for two dirhams; rather dirham for dirham and dinar for dinar (should be equal), with no difference between them except in weight."
"7725","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not proper for any human being to prostrate to another human being; and if it were proper for a human being to prostrate to another human being, I would have commanded the woman to prostrate to her husband, because of the greatness of his right over her. By the One in whose Hand is my soul, if the husband had a wound from his feet to the parting of his hair, oozing with pus and blood, and the wife then began to lick it, even then she would not have fulfilled his right."
"7726","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should pray in a single garment while no part of it is over his shoulder."
"7727","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The imam should not pray (a voluntary prayer) in the same place where he prayed the obligatory prayer until he moves (from his place)."
"7728","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Prayer is not to be offered in the resting places of camels, but prayer may be offered in the pens of sheep and goats."
"7729","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should pray with his hair tied back (in a knot)."
"7730","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should fast on Friday alone, unless he (also) fasts a day before it or a day after it."
"7731","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a thorn pricks the believer, or something greater than that befalls him, Allah raises him a degree because of it and wipes away a sin from him."
"7732","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whatever affliction befalls a servant, whether small or great, befalls him only because of some sin, and what Allah forgives is even more than that."
"7733","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Nothing makes anything else sick (by itself); so who gave the mange to the first animal? There is no contagion (in reality) and no Safar (its ill omen has no reality). Allah created every soul and wrote down its life, its provision and its afflictions."
"7734","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should slander another."
"7735","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should take a ritual bath (ghusl) in stagnant water while in a state of major ritual impurity (janabah)."
"7736","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any man who takes a ritual bath (ghusl) on Friday, purifies himself as much as he can, applies his oil or uses the perfume of his house, then goes out (to the mosque), does not separate two people, then prays whatever has been written for him, then remains silent when the imam delivers the sermon, (his sins) between that and the next Friday are forgiven."
"7737","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not let the adhan of Bilal deceive you regarding your sahur (pre-dawn meal), nor the whiteness on the horizon that stretches lengthwise, until it spreads (across the breadth)."
"7738","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer does not commit betrayal."
"7739","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Caution cannot avert destiny, and supplication benefits against the affliction that has already descended and against that which has not yet descended; and indeed, the affliction descends and supplication meets it, and the two continue to wrestle with each other until the Day of Resurrection."
"7740","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two (parties to a transaction) should part only with mutual consent."
"7741","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No believing man should hate a believing woman; if he dislikes one of her traits, he will be pleased with another."
"7742","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever vomits, or has a wet dream, or has himself cupped, his fast is not broken."
"7743","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever completes the Qur'an in less than three days does not understand it (properly)."
"7744","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Retaliation (qisas) shall not be taken from a father for his child."
"7745","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the ablution of one of you is broken, Allah does not accept his prayer until he performs ablution."
"7746","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity given from wealth obtained through betrayal (of trust)."
"7747","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah does not accept the prayer of a woman who has reached puberty without a head-covering (covering her head)."
"7748","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty does not accept any deed from a polytheist who returns to associating partners (with Allah) after having become Muslim, until he leaves the polytheists and joins the Muslims."
"7749","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A father shall not be killed in retaliation for his child."
"7750","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After this day, until the Day of Resurrection, no Qurayshi will be bound and killed (without a crime)."
"7751","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer shall not be killed in retaliation for a disbeliever, nor shall one under a covenant (be killed) during the term of his covenant."
"7752","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A Muslim shall not be killed in retaliation for a disbeliever."
"7753","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None gives sermons and admonition except a ruler, or a person appointed by him, or a self-conceited man."
"7754","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None preaches to the people except a ruler, or a person appointed by him, or a show-off."
"7755","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A judge should not judge between two parties while he is angry."
"7756","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one should give two different judgments in one matter, and no one should judge between two parties while he is angry."
"7757","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever people sit to remember Allah, the angels surround them, mercy covers them, tranquility (sakinah) descends upon them, and Allah mentions them among those who are with Him (the angels)."
"7758","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should say (to his slave): 'Feed your lord, help your lord perform ablution, give your lord water to drink,' and no one should say: 'My lord,' rather let him say: 'My master and my patron.' And none of you should say: 'My slave and my slave-girl,' rather let him say: 'My young man, my young woman and my servant.'"
"7759","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should say, 'My soul has become wicked,' rather let him say, 'My soul is nauseated.'"
"7760","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should say, 'I forgot such-and-such a verse,' rather (it should be said that) he was made to forget it."
"7761","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should call (the grapevine) 'karm' (generosity), for karm is the Muslim man; rather, call (it) grape gardens."
"7762","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should make his brother get up from his place on Friday and then sit in his place himself; rather let him say: 'Make room.'"
"7763","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should say: 'O Allah, forgive me if You will; O Allah, have mercy on me if You will; O Allah, provide for me if You will.' Rather, let him ask with firm resolve, for Allah does whatever He wills; there is no one who can compel Him."
"7764","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should say that I am better than Yunus bin Matta."
"7765","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should say: 'My slave and my slave-girl.' All of you are slaves of Allah and all your women are bondswomen of Allah. Rather, let him say: 'My servant, my maidservant, my young man and my young woman.'"
"7766","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should say: 'My slave' or 'my slave-girl,' nor should a slave say: 'My lord' and 'my lady.' Rather, let the owner say: 'My young man and my young woman,' and let the slave say: 'My master and my mistress,' for you are all owned, and the Lord is only Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"7767","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should call the grape 'karm' (generosity), for the real karm is the heart of the believer."
"7768","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should say: 'O the misfortune of time!' for Allah is time (its Creator and Controller)."
"7769","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should stand for prayer while he is in discomfort (from holding back urine or stool)."
"7770","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man should not make another man get up from his place and then sit there himself."
"7771","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man should not make another man get up from his place and then sit there himself; rather make room (among yourselves) or make space."
"7772","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is wounded in the path of Allah, and Allah knows best who is wounded in His path, will come on the Day of Resurrection with his wound gushing blood; its colour will be the colour of blood, but its fragrance will be the fragrance of musk."
"7773","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Those who curse frequently will be neither intercessors nor witnesses on the Day of Resurrection."
"7774","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer is not one who curses frequently."
"7775","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a Muslim to stay estranged from a Muslim for more than three days. So when he meets him and greets him with salam three times, and each time he does not reply, then (the one who refuses to reconcile) returns with his own sin."
"7776","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever plots against the people of Madinah will dissolve just as salt dissolves in water."
"7777","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one in ihram should not wear a shirt, a turban, trousers, a hooded cloak, or a garment touched by wars or saffron, nor should he wear leather socks, unless he cannot find sandals, in which case he may wear the leather socks, but he should cut them so that they are below the ankles."
"7778","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man who weeps out of fear of Allah will not enter Hell until milk returns into the udder (that is, never), and the dust of the path of Allah and the smoke of Hell can never be gathered together in the nostrils of a Muslim."
"7779","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer is not stung from the same hole twice."
"7780","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None should touch the Qur'an except one who is pure."
"7781","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should hold his private part with his right hand while urinating, nor clean himself with his right hand after relieving himself, nor breathe into the vessel."
"7782","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should walk wearing one sandal or one leather sock; either wear both or take both off."
"7783","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should withhold surplus water in order thereby to withhold the pasture (by taking control of it)."
"7784","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No neighbour should prevent his neighbour from fixing a wooden beam in his wall."
"7785","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Surplus water should not be withheld, nor should the excess water of a well be withheld."
"7786","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let not the adhan of Bilal prevent any of you from eating his suhur, for he calls the adhan while it is still night, so that the one among you standing in prayer may go back (to rest) and the one sleeping may wake up. And the dawn (light) is not like this (lengthwise); rather it is like this (widthwise), spreading across the horizon of the sky."
"7787","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a Muslim dies and a group of Muslims numbering one hundred or more offer the funeral prayer over him and intercede for him, their intercession for him is accepted."
"7788","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever a Muslim man dies, Allah admits a Jew or a Christian into Hell in his place."
"7789","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""As long as I am present among you, inform me whenever anyone among you dies, for my (funeral) prayer over him is a mercy for him."
"7790","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any woman among you whose three children die and who bears it patiently hoping for reward will enter Paradise, and in the case of two children as well (the same ruling applies)."
"7791","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If three of a Muslim's children die, he will not enter Hellfire, except to the extent of fulfilling the oath."
"7792","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should die except in the state that he holds a good opinion of Allah Almighty."
"7793","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In disobedience to Allah, in severing ties of kinship, and in what you do not have authority over, no oath is binding on you, nor any vow."
"7794","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not proper for anyone to have an engraving made like the engraving of this ring of mine."
"7795","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not proper for a truthful friend to be one who curses a great deal."
"7796","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not proper for any servant to say: I am better than Yunus bin Matta."
"7797","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not proper for a believer to humiliate himself: (that is,) to expose himself to a trial that he does not have the strength to bear."
"7798","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This (that is, silk) is not proper for the God-fearing."
"7799","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two people should not converse privately, leaving out the third, because that grieves him (the third)."
"7800","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No man should look at the private parts of another man, nor should any woman look at the private parts of another woman; and no man should lie skin to skin with another man under a single garment, nor should any woman lie skin to skin with another woman under a single garment."
"7801","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah does not look (with the look of mercy) at a man who approaches a man or a woman in the rear (anus)."
"7802","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah does not look at a man who has intercourse with his wife in her rear (anus)."
"7803","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah does not look at the one who drags his garment (on the ground) out of arrogance."
"7804","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, Allah will not look at the one who drags his lower garment (on the ground) out of arrogance."
"7805","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one (performing Hajj) should depart until his last act is the circumambulation (tawaf) of the House of Allah."
"7806","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This (deed) will not benefit him, because he never once said: O my Lord, forgive me my sin on the Day of Judgement."
"7807","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one should have an engraving made like the engraving of this ring of mine."
"7808","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A fornicator who has been flogged should marry only someone like himself (a fornicatress)."
"7809","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one in the state of ihram should not marry himself, nor arrange anyone else's marriage, nor make a proposal of marriage."
"7810","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The owner of sick (camels) should not bring his sick animals to the healthy ones."
